      <item>
         <title><![CDATA[Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time's gorgeous remake retains the original's soul]]></title>
         <link>https://www.cbc.ca/news/entertainment/zelda-ocarina-remake-review-9.7405039?cmp=rss</link>
         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/9a2a555c-7731-4f8b-b92d-e1baa550a714,1793648832923/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%28369%2C139%2C1254%2C705%29%3B' alt='A man in a green tunic and cap holds a longsword in the air.' width='620' height='349' title='The Hero of Time, Link, holds the Master Sword in the remake of Nintendo&apos;s classic adventure, The Legend of Zelda: The Ocarina of Time.'/><p>Nearly 30 years after the original, Nintendo has remade The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time. It’s an unquestionable fan favourite that’s shinier, but retains the soul of a game that isn’t made like this anymore.</p>]]></description>
