      <item>
         <title><![CDATA[Prime Minister says Russia will not be allowed to compete at 2026 world juniors in Alberta]]></title>
         <link>https://www.cbc.ca/sports/hockey/norway-hockey-world-championships-refusal-russia-9.7406832?cmp=rss</link>
         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/2684e265-2951-42d7-b1f7-5b2063472513,1793745944968/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C51%2C3747%2C2107%29%3B' alt='Prime Minister Mark Carney stands during an executive session.' width='620' height='349' title='Prime Minister Mark Carney is seen arriving to an executive session of the 28th Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting, in St. John&apos;s, Antigua and Barbuda on Tuesday.'/><p>Prime Minister Mark Carney says Russia will not be allowed to compete at next month's world junior hockey championship in Alberta. Carney, speaking in Antigua at the Commonwealth Summit, said Russian and Belarusian athletes will not be permitted to represent their countries in Canada as long as the war in Ukraine continues.</p>]]></description>
         <pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 06:49:14 EST</pubDate>
         <category>Sports/Hockey</category>
         <guid isPermaLink="false">9.7406832</guid>
         <dc:type>story</dc:type>
         <dc:rights>Syndication Allowed</dc:rights>
      </item>
      <item>
         <title><![CDATA[Home in Amherstburg, Ont., unlivable after family spent $155K on renovations, police looking for contractor]]></title>
         <link>https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/windsor/amherstburg-renovations-police-seeking-contractor-9.7407157?cmp=rss</link>
         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/577ce90c-43d2-429a-9819-8da65a2f1b7f,1793728105524/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C62%2C5712%2C3213%29%3B' alt='Tonya Azevedo stands in the backyard of her Alma Street home that her family cannot currently live because of unsafe work that was done during renovations.' width='620' height='349' title='Amherstburg, Ont., resident Tonya Azevedo stands in the backyard of her Alma Street home that her family can&apos;t live in because of unsafe work done during renovations.'/><p>Tonya Azevedo says she lost $155,000 and her family of four can no longer live in their home of 20 years after a contractor who told them he was licensed did work that turned out to be unsafe. “I’m absolutely heartbroken,” says Azevedo, who had remortgaged her home to pay for the renos.</p>]]></description>
